# Duckpond — hardest to easiest

Started 2026-09-06; updated 2026-09-07. Preserve the broad main chat layout.
User constraint: do not load or run models yet. No inference, cloning-quality tests,
weight downloads, or performance benchmarks until the user resumes that work.

1. Media backend compatibility and model lifecycle
   - [x] Classify architecture/task/runtime and detect incomplete local weights.
   - [x] Strict explicit selection; no silent cross-task model substitution.
   - [x] Repair diffusion dispatch, music duration/rate, seed 0, cancellation paths.
   - [x] Reuse resident models and inference mode without shrinking context.
   - [x] Synthetic cache and fake pipeline regression tests.
   - [ ] Add dedicated GGUF media and conditioning-image/video adapters.
   - [ ] Validate compatible downloaded weights on actual hardware (deferred).
2. Durable chat and agent jobs, timeouts, and hidden limits
   - [ ] Trace app, llama router, native runtime, tunnel, and provider timeouts.
   - [ ] Persist resumable job checkpoints across server/deployment restarts.
   - [ ] Review agent step/research limits, reasoning watchdog, output caps, and
         command timeouts; make appropriate limits visible/configurable and
         recoverable instead of cutting off productive work without explanation.
   - [x] Source-only deployment detection; drain admission and wait for active
         requests, agent jobs, downloads and embedding backfills before restart.
   - [ ] Activate deployment guard in the live process during the next controlled
         restart; legacy health responses defer automatically until then.
   - [x] Preserve context accounting in reconnect snapshots; initialize counts
         before decoding and consume prompt timings; ignore stale count fetches.
   - [ ] Complete live counts for all remote/agent routes and test long turns.
   - [ ] Reproduce the reported history disappearance after errors; verify saved
         tree/branch/partial-work recovery through disconnects and process exit.
   - [x] Isolate individual message render failures with a raw-text fallback.
   - Local Cloudflare operational notes: /home/cranky/Desktop/cloudflair.txt.
     Contains credentials: never copy into source, logs, commits, or handoff notes.
